      "question": {
        ":question/id": "618f58a8-e1e1-5e32-9c15-6b3c70021057",
        ":question/problem": "Let\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $4\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}={BA}_{4\\times 4}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
